<title>USA: Wabash National Corp Q4 net, sales lower.</title>
<headline>Wabash National Corp Q4 net, sales lower.</headline>
<dateline>LAFAYETTE, Ind. 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fourth Quarter		   Year</p>
<p>			  1996	  1995	   1996	 1995</p>
<p> Net Sales	 $168,361    $187,087     $631,492   $734,299</p>
<p> Gross Profit	 7,807	10,852	 28,863     56,796</p>
<p>Income From Operations</p>
<p>			  4,468	 8,109	 15,504     45,935</p>
<p>Income Before Taxes</p>
<p>			  2,101	 5,904	  6,035     40,309</p>
<p> Net Income	   1,237	 4,562	  3,638     25,407</p>
<p> Net Per Share	 0.07	  0.24	   0.19	 1.34</p>
<p>Avg Shrs Out  18,908,000  18,961,000   18,912,000 18,948,000</p>
<p>(Dollars in Thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE: Lower 1996 Q4 net reflects deferral of earnings associated with $35 million of equipment which went out on operating lease by its Wabash National Finance Corp leasing subsidiary.  These earnings will be recognized over the term of the lease.  In addition, the company said it did not have enough of a new product to meet demand.</p>
<p>	   ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
</text>
